    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0886" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg816"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Harris.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 20.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 7, 1861.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of June 7 (No. 21) has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>It affords the President sincere pleasure to know that the government of the
                    Tycoon has exerted so much diligence to bring the assassins of Mr. Heusken to
                    punishment, and that you are satisfied that those exertions have been made with
                    good faith. It is expected that the government will not abate its efforts until
                    the end so important to a good understanding between the two countries shall
                    have been attained.</p>
                <p>The punishment of the delinquent Yakonines, who were in attendance on the
                    deceased when the crime was committed, is regarded by this government with high
                    approbation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Townsend Harris,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Yedo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
